WEBVTT

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:09.880
Did we get it?

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.010
What?!

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.170
We're safe now, Tiffa.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.130
What's the matter, Tiffa?

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.640
A Gundam-type, huh? I'm dying to take this guy on.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.060
Good grief. Fine, be my guest.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.900
Gundams? Two of them?

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.780
Is the Moon out?

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.370
I asked you if the Moon is out!

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.300
Here they come!

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:43.930
<b>After War</b>

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:43.930
<b>GUNDAM</b>

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:51.440
<b>The dream I'd nearly forgotten is beginning to stir,</b>

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.400
<b>little by little</b>

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.950
<b>filling in the gaps in my heart</b>

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:06.330
<b>The instant my frozen memories begin to awaken,</b>

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:15.880
<b>my only wish is for the future that is about to begin</b>

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:19.380
<b>I'll reach out with both hands</b>

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.390
<b>and embrace that dream I once had</b>

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:27.060
<b>I want to go on believing</b>

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.940
<b>without ever letting go or giving up</b>

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:34.570
<b>Until the day comes when I grab hold...</b>

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:38.400
<b>...of that dream I once had,</b>

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.990
<b>I want to keep chasing after it</b>

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:47.830
<b>without ever forgetting my hopes and dreams</b>

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:58.260
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:58.260
<b>"I Will Give You Power"</b>

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.140
Here they come!

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.860
Looks like I'm finally gonna be able to fight somebody who's worth my time!

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.570
Roabea, you hang back!

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.490
Witz always gets so worked up...

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:31.580
Aren't adults supposed to do their job, collect their pay, and then go home?

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.670
A-Are there weapons? Is this it?

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:53.770
I thought I told you to hang back!

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.610
I'm on the clock, too.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.070
Th-They're coming for us?

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.070
Okay, let's try this!

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.120
Listen up, you two!

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.290
What the hell?!

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.910
That sounded like a kid!

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.370
If you keep attacking me, something horrible will happen!

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:17.840
Listen up, and listen good!

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:22.470
This Gundam is equipped with a terrifying secret weapon!

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.930
If you don't want to be on the receiving end-

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.850
You stupid kid! Like anybody would fall for a bluff like that!

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.850
It's not nice to tell lies, kiddo!

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.110
Crap, I should've known that would be too obvious...

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.740
Sara, put me through to those two.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:49.700
Yes, sir.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.910
Your objective is only the retrieval of Tiffa Adill.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.370
Avoid any attacks that might hit the cockpit directly.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.550
Don't shoot the cockpit?

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:02.460
Fine, whatever you say.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.300
Oh, those guys must be trying to take you back!

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:09.640
In which case...

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:16.440
Wait!

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:17.400
What?!

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:22.400
Okay, let's try this again! Shoot at me, I dare you!

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:31.200
I knew it, you can't shoot! This girl is what you're really after!

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.080
That's a dirty stunt he's pulling...

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.000
He's clever, I'll give him that.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.840
Don't forget that I'm the one with the Ace of Hearts!

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.460
See ya!

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:50.300
Damn it, nobody messes with me!

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:51.930
Oh, dear.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.980
He can fly, too?!

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.270
I have you now!

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:07.900
What the hell?!

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.200
"Do not pursue," huh?

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:28.300
I'm sorry. I didn't scare you too much, did I?

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:32.430
I... trust you.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:44.650
I'm heading back to the Freeden. Our contract covers maintenance.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.320
Their mechanics are pretty good.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.860
I'll take a break, too.

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:54.530
If I don't step back and count to ten, I'm gonna lose it.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:08.170
Looks like I'll be able to afford some good booze for once.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:24.360
There's no telling when they'll show up again.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.770
Gotta fill up while I can...

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:30.610
We need to get past those guys, and then...

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:34.910
Hang on, what do we do after that?

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:37.870
You're done already?

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.000
No, I'm fine.

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:44.040
If you insist...

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.550
I thought I was a goner there!

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.940
There are those who live in the nighttime world.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:06.940
Mobile suit pilots on the hunt for prey,

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:10.440
as well as information brokers out selling their latest intel to Vultures.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:15.870
They too, dwell in the world of the night.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:25.330
A Gundam-type that no one's ever seen before?

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:29.670
You mean the one that rumor says is some old U.N.E. secret weapon?

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.670
Almost certainly.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:35.840
Plus, the person at the controls doesn't seem to be a mobile suit pilot.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.430
So, this is the Gundam?

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:42.430
Capture it undamaged, and you could be an invincible mobile suit pilot.

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:46.230
And even if you smashed it, you could name your own price for its electronics.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:49.520
Even a single arm or leg would be worth a mint.

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:52.320
That's how it is with Gundams.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:54.860
I've uploaded the details onto this.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:56.740
I suggest you buy now.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:59.370
Or someone will beat me to it?

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:01.410
I'm a businessman.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.120
All right, fine!

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.040
Always a pleasure!

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:25.850
Don't you think it's strange?

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:31.070
Jamil Neate has a pretty solid rep in the Vulture world, right?

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:35.740
Why is a guy like Jamil so hell-bent on getting one little girl back?

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:37.610
My point exactly.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:42.830
That raid on the Alternative Company the other day was pretty hardcore, too

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:46.040
I don't know what he's up to, and I don't really care.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.420
Really? That's a shame.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:52.590
If we figured out her secret, we could parlay that into-

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.340
We could use it to make some money?!

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:57.760
Keep your voice down! What if someone hears?

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.220
Someone did, actually. What about it?

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:05.810
This is why freelancers are so risky. They'll turn on you in a second.

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:07.690
I'm reporting you to the Captain.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:10.400
Hey, wait!

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:12.690
Save your excuses for the Captain.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.110
Has anyone told you that you're lovely when you're angry?

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:20.410
Hey, I said to wait!

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:24.120
You risked your lives to nab that girl, but were kept in the dark like us, right?

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.330
Th-That's because he-

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:30.120
The Captain's a tight-lipped guy.

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:33.210
We earn our living by putting our lives on the line.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:38.920
We at least want to know who that Tiffa girl is.

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:46.470
Tiffa, where were you before those guys grabbed you?

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:50.310
And what's the deal with that strange power of yours?

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:57.070
I wonder if the people with superpowers who fought in the war were like you.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:03.740
Hey, I'll never learn about you if you don't say anything.

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:06.290
I...

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.290
I want to know about you.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:14.960
Okay.

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:20.840
I was born in the year the war ended.

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:27.260
My old man was an engineer who worked for the military.

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:29.310
He died in the war.

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:34.020
In my earliest memories, things were still a mess.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:38.280
The sun never came out, and it was always like winter.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:42.360
Around half of my friends died from various causes.

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:46.870
When it seemed like spring had finally come,

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:49.700
I decided that I wanted to be an engineer.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:55.040
I guess I take after my old man, 'cause I've always had a knack for it.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:02.260
But one day, my town got attacked by wandering mobile suit pilots.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:07.760
It was a miracle that I survived.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:12.060
Actually, I think I really did die for a bit that day.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:15.690
That let me make a clean start.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:18.230
Anyway, that's how I got into this line of work.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:28.530
Those were sad times... Even memories are sad.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:34.540
I'm... alone, too.

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:37.210
Tiffa...

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:40.460
Warm... hands.

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:49.760
Say, Tiffa... If we... If we manage to give these guys the slip...

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:53.980
Hypothetically speaking, maybe you and I could...

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.190
What?!

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:03.690
I've found my prize!

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:13.250
Goodbye, you kids.

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:33.680
Now!

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:38.270
Other pilots?!

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.410
Wh-What the heck?!

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.910
What's with all these mobile suits?!

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:06.630
I'm not about to hand it over!

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:09.260
I'm the one who found it!

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.690
I have you now!

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.020
What?!

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:37.660
I almost had it!

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:50.630
In a world where order has broken down, only your own strength can be trusted.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:54.510
To survive, one must fight.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:01.980
The war was indeed over.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:07.360
But many individual wars raged on.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:19.160
Get plenty of stills! We can milk that Gundam for more money!

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:25.590
Info! Info is everything! Control that, and you'll make a fortune!

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:32.300
I have to say, we humans are an ugly bunch!

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:36.050
Even after a war like that, we go on fighting!

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:41.560
But us smart types watch from a safe distance and reap the profits.

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:50.860
Captain! What appears to be battle flashes spotted at

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.630
The cockpit!

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:02.660
Smash the cockpit!

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:04.580
I'm not gonna lose!

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:10.590
I'm not about to die in a place like this!

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:13.630
I'm not about to die!

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:17.260
I'm not gonna let her die!

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.020
Garrod...

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:29.190
We'll reach the combat area in five minutes. Please get ready.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:32.400
Ready whenever you are. Hey, has anybody ever told you-

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:34.780
Did you get that?

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:38.240
I know how to do my job! Get off my back, you nag!

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:41.700
Honestly, all men who pilot mobile suits are jerks.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:43.870
Listen, you two.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.420
Do your best, all right?

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:17.070
Crap, is this the end of the line?

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:19.160
Garrod.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:23.040
I will give you power.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.660
Power?

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:56.990
I don't believe it... Launch mobile suits!

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.740
Stop what you're doing, Tiffa!

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.010
Stand aside, people!

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:22.430
Don't get in our way!

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:32.560
Wh-What's this mean?

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:36.230
"Satellite System"?

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:43.160
This is the power you meant?

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:45.870
Okay... Is this how it works?!

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:53.420
What's that?

00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:55.880
A laser signal? From the Moon?

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:07.560
Tiffa, please hear my voice...

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:10.770
I can't reach her?

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:20.570
And next a microwave is coming 4.03 seconds from now?

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:22.700
It's coming.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:19:59.320
Don't shoot!

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:01.700
Get 'em!

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:40.610
Wh-What in the world is that?

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:42.690
I have no idea...

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:44.860
A nightmare.

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:49.490
A nightmare from 15 years ago.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:38.290
Th-That's the power of this Gundam?

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:53.270
But hey, we're alive! Right, Tiffa?

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:56.770
Tiffa?

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:06.240
That Gundam is seriously scary...

00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:09.740
Yeah, that's not something for a kid to be messing with.

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:19.040
Too many people have died.

00:22:20.630 --> 00:22:23.380
Tiffa, you're going to-

00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:32.300
What's wrong, Tiffa?! Tiffa!

00:22:36.220 --> 00:22:38.640
Tiffa!

00:22:46.110 --> 00:22:51.410
<b>Can I find the words to tell you</b>

00:22:49.120 --> 00:22:53.850
The deaths of so many has dealt a blow to Tiffa's psyche.

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:56.790
<b>How I live between the walls of steel and stone</b>

00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:57.070
When Jamil recovers Tiffa in a flashy manner,

00:22:57.070 --> 00:23:00.920
he takes Garrod prisoner along with the Gundam X.

00:22:58.460 --> 00:23:04.630
<b>How I close my eyes to find some kind of rapture</b>

00:23:00.920 --> 00:23:04.790
But Garrod's purehearted devotion remains undeterred.

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:10.970
<b>In a world where you can feel so all alone</b>

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:17.970
<b>Inside I'm full of light and laughter</b>

00:23:19.430 --> 00:23:21.850
<b>There's a flame that burns in me</b>

00:23:21.850 --> 00:23:22.810
<b>(I need a way)</b>

00:23:22.810 --> 00:23:26.900
<b>(I need a way) I need a way to set it free</b>

00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:31.820
<b>When you find love in your heart</b>

00:23:31.820 --> 00:23:33.950
<b>(The human touch)</b>

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:37.990
<b>You can believe from the start</b>

00:23:37.990 --> 00:23:40.000
<b>(From the start)</b>

00:23:40.910 --> 00:23:43.120
<b>Dreams they come true</b>

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:44.500
<b>(They come true)</b>

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:48.840
<b>All comes to you, oh all at once</b>

00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:52.630
<b>If you believe in human touch</b>

00:23:50.510 --> 00:23:52.880
My steed is vicious.

00:23:52.880 --> 00:23:56.760
<b>Episode 3</b>

00:23:52.880 --> 00:23:56.760
<b>"My Steed is Vicious"</b>

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:58.760
<b></b>
